# Frontend environment variables (Vite)
#
# Copy to `frontend/.env.local` for local development. `.env*` files are
# gitignored — never commit real values.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# -----------------
# Leave VITE_API_BASE_URL unset. The Vite dev server proxies /api and /login
# (and other backend paths) to the Django API on port 8001, so the browser
# sends cookies to the API origin and no environment variable is needed.
#
# PRODUCTION (Vercel)
# ------------------
# Set VITE_API_BASE_URL to the deployed Render API URL, e.g.
# https://<your-app>.onrender.com  (replace <your-app> with your app name).
# This is the ONLY Vite environment variable that must be configured in
# production — it points the client at the API origin.
#
# IMPORTANT: never commit real values. The variable is read at build time
# and baked into the bundle, so set it in the Vercel project environment,
# not in a committed .env file.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=
